# Internationalization and localization documentation

Documentation must describe behavior under language, locale, and directionality changes.

## Component pages (`docs/components/*.md`)

- `## Usage Guidelines` -> `### Behavior` must explicitly address:
  - RTL/LTR behavior,
  - text expansion/compression risk,
  - locale-dependent formats when applicable (dates, numbers, currency).
- If any item is unknown, set it to `TBD` and add a matching item in `## Gaps / TBD`.

## Pattern/workflow pages (`docs/workflows/**/*.md`)

- Pattern behavior must include i18n/l10n decision notes:
  - what mirrors in RTL,
  - what must not mirror,
  - string-length stress cases,
  - locale format dependencies.
- Include at least one failure mode caused by localization and the expected fallback.

## Foundation pages (`docs/foundations/*.md`)

- For typography/content-related foundations, include:
  - text expansion guidance,
  - line-height implications for non-Latin scripts,
  - truncation policy references when available.

## Motion and zoom resilience

- For interactive patterns/components, document:
  - expected behavior under reduced-motion preference (`prefers-reduced-motion`),
  - expected behavior under zoomed layouts (200% baseline).
- If not yet verified, use `TBD (pending i18n/a11y verification)`.

## Prohibited omissions

- Do not imply i18n or RTL support without explicit behavior notes.
- Do not claim localization readiness solely from token support.

